    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nAfter updating to latest version of the plugin I have problems with the explorer closing itself after maybe 1 second after moving one step in the tree (in or out).\r\nI have remapped the keys so it looks like this:\r\n```\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t-- File manager\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.files\",\r\n\t\tversion = false,\r\n\t\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\t\trequire(\"mini.files\").setup({\r\n\t\t\t\tmappings = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tgo_in_plus = \"<Right>\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\tgo_out_plus = \"<Left>\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\tsynchronize = \"<C-s>\",\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t})\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t\tevent = \"VeryLazy\",\r\n\t},\r\n```\r\nThis worked perfectly before I updated.\r\n\r\nI tried looking at checkHealth to see if there were any conflicts but found nothing to explain this.\r\n\r\nIf I try using the default movements (h and l) it works as expected.\r\n\r\nI tried using just go_in and go_out and it makes no difference.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. ...\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThat using my mappings does not close the explorer until the last node is a file or I exit the explorer.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe explorer closing itself after maybe 1 second after moving one step in the tree (in or out).",
